  "title": "The Helpful Stranger Wants a Code",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "consumer digital literacy",
  "premise": "An account owner wants to solve an access problem, but an unsolicited helper asks them to read out a sign-in code. A boundary between official recovery and incoming requests stops the disclosure and redirects to a verified support route.",
  "hook": "What would this code let the stranger do?",
  "visible_action": "A masked code card approaches an outgoing message slot, stops at a verification barrier, and remains concealed.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Treat authentication codes as part of a specific sign-in, not proof for an unsolicited helper.",
  "gate": "Verify provider guidance; show no real code and give no impersonation script or account-recovery bypass.",
